    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass, build succeeds. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed on creation.\n\n**Formula** (per spec): start at 1, +1 if an email is present, +1 if `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (level 4 reserved for tenure). For the test owner (email present, unique name \u2192 namesakeCount 0): 1 + 1 + 1 = 3. \u2713\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the read-only `membershipTier` string schema with a `membershipLevel` integer (`int32`, min 1, max 3). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field, so the old field is gone from the response.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 retargeted the mapping to `membershipLevel` and replaced the `membershipTier(...)` GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE method with `membershipLevel(Owner)` implementing the numeric rule. Kept the same \"compute from stored fields at map time\" pattern the tier used, so both the create response and later `GET` return the same value.\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 the create audit line now records the level: it injects `OwnerMapper` (a Spring bean via `mapstruct.defaultComponentModel=spring`) and appends `membershipLevel={}` to the audit message, keeping a single source of truth for the computation. Verified in the run: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 ... membershipLevel=3`.\n\n4. **`AssignOwnerHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 updated a stale doc comment that referenced the removed `membershipTier`/GOLD rule (`householdSize` is no longer part of the level calculation).\n\nNo lingering `membershipTier` references remain anywhere in `src/`.",
